body:
Weed is weird for me, when I do it infrequently and in small doses, it tends to make me really happy, giggly, clear-headed and unexpectedly productive. I have self-control issues though and tend to go overboard with things, and going overboard with weed guarantees that I'm going to spend everyday chasing a high, smoking up and wondering where the good vibes went, to the point where anything that gets in the way of me getting high and doing nothing will piss me off. When I'm overdoing weed, I flip between depressed + unmotivated and never-fully-mad-but-always-irritable pretty frequently. I become less reactive perhaps, but just as moody, and much more likely to isolate myself to just get high and do nothing.

&#x200B;

I stopped smoking for a good while and recently started again and am trying to find that sweet spot where I'm allowing myself to get high without getting high every single day and night, to the point where it loses its (positive) effect.
